ists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-05-16T13:14:08Z","updated_at":"2016-05-16T13:14:08Z","body":"After executing `gradle --info :junit-tests:junit5Test`, I consistently see the following:\n\n```\n:junit-tests:junit5Test\nExecuting task ':junit-tests:junit5Test' (up-to-date check took 0.002 secs) due to:\n  Input file /Users/sbrannen/source/junit-lambda/junit4-runner/build/libs/junit4-runner-5.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar has changed.\n  Input file /Users/sbrannen/source/junit-lambda/junit-commons/build/libs/junit-commons-5.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar has changed.\n  Input file /Users/sbrannen/source/junit-lambda/junit5-engine/build/libs/junit5-engine-5.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar has changed.\n```\n\nCan anyone enlighten me as to why `junit4-runner-5.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar`, `junit-commons-5.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar`, and `junit5-engine-5.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar` would have been _changed_? \n\nFrom my understanding, those JARs should not be rebuilt if nothing has changed in those projects.\n\nNote, however, that when I execute `gradle -a :junit-tests:junit5Test` things work as expected.\n\nSo I guess the real question is: _How can we modify the build so that the JARs from other projects are not modified unnecessarily?_\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/comments/219421585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"com